  "english_paragraphs": [
    "A man was passing through a busy train station when he saw a person with a disability selling things. He casually dropped a hundred yuan in front of him. Before long, though, he came back and apologized: “I’m sorry. You’re a businessperson, but I treated you like a beggar.”",
    "Some time later, the man passed through the station again. A shop owner smiled and called out to him from the doorway. “I’ve been hoping to see you again,” said the person he had met before. “You were the first person to treat me like a businessperson. Look at me now—I really am one.”",
    "Make an effort to respect everyone. Your respect may have a positive effect on someone else."
  ],
  "english_full": "A man was passing through a busy train station when he saw a person with a disability selling things. He casually dropped a hundred yuan in front of him. Before long, though, he came back and apologized: “I’m sorry. You’re a businessperson, but I treated you like a beggar.”\n\nSome time later, the man passed through the station again. A shop owner smiled and called out to him from the doorway. “I’ve been hoping to see you again,” said the person he had met before. “You were the first person to treat me like a businessperson. Look at me now—I really am one.”\n\nMake an effort to respect everyone. Your respect may have a positive effect on someone else.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "О́дин муж проходи́л чрез за́нятый вокза́л, когда́ он уви́дел осо́бу с неправоспосо́бностью, продаю́щую предме́ты. Он слу́чайно уро́нил со́тню юа́нь пе́ред ним. Долгими́ не бы́ли хлопоты, как он верну́лся и извиня́лся: \"Мне жаль. Ты бизнесме́н, а я обошёлся с тобо́й, как с нищебро́дом.\"",
    "Через какóе-то вре́мя муж про́шёл через вокза́л снова́. Владеле́ц магази́на улы́бнулся и позва́л его́ из дверно́го проёма. \"Я наде́ялся, что увижу тебя́ снова,\" ска́зал тот, кого он ранее́ встреча́л. \"Ты был пе́рвым, кто обошёлся со мной, как с бизнесме́ном. Посмотри́ на меня́ сейча́с—я действи́тельно бизнесме́н.\"",
    "Прилага́йте уси́лие, чтобы уважать всех. Ваше уваже́ние может дать пoзити́вный эффе́кт на кого́-то друго́го."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Ódin muzh prokhodíl chrez zányaty vokzál, kogdá on uvídel osóbu s nepravosposóbnost'yu, prodayúshchuyu predméty. On slucháino urónil sótnyu yuáń péred nim. Dolgimí ne býli khlopoty, kak on vernúlsya i izvinílsya: \"Mne zhal'. Ty biznesmén, a ya oboshólsya s tobóy, kak s nishchebródom.\"",
    "Cherez kakóe-to vremya muzh próshël chrez vokzál snová. Vladélets magazína ulýbnulsya i pozvál egó iz dvernógo próyema. \"Ya nadéyalsya, chto uvízhu tebá snova,\" skázal tot, kogo on rán'ye vstrechá́l. \"Ty byl pérvym, kto oboshólsya so mnoy, kak s biznesmén. Posmotrí na menyá seychás—ya deystvítel'no biznesmén.\"",
    "Prilagáyte usíliye, chtoby uvazhát' vsekh. Vashe uvazhéniye mozhet dat' pozitívnyy éffekt na kogó-to drugógo."
  ],
